      "title": "Nonlinear Component Analysis as a Kernel Eigenvalue Problem",
      "abstract": "<jats:p> A new method for performing a nonlinear form of principal component analysis is proposed. By the use of integral operator kernel functions, one can efficiently compute principal components in high-dimensional feature spaces, related to input space by some nonlinear map\u2014for instance, the space of all possible five-pixel products in 16 \u00d7 16 images. We give the derivation of the method and present experimental results on polynomial feature extraction for pattern recognition. </jats:p>",
